From 3df261503882636045c170ecea196a0267e23fba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:46:09 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] video: give a WebView's video a layer of its own

init.xenvm-webview.rc writes the WebView's command line with
WebViewSurfaceControl and WebViewThreadSafeMedia, which make a <video>
element's video a SurfaceControl of its own, so drm_hwcomposer can put
it on a plane instead of SurfaceFlinger drawing it into the app's
window: dropped frames 16% -> 1.7% for a local 1080p30 H.264 video on
this board over 5 minutes (2026-10-03, the file put there by hand). The
product makefile installs the rc, and README.md lists it.

It works only while the product boots permissive: creating a file in
/data/local/tmp is a neverallow for vendor_init and for init itself
(system/sepolicy/private/vendor_init.te:365, init.te:853), so no init
script on any partition can write it in enforcing; the rc says what
to do then (write it once with adb shell; it stays in /data). Not yet
run from this makefile on a board.

DomaNoSafeAreaRRO, a product RRO on CarSystemUI, sets
config_enableSafeAreaAndToolbarPerDisplay to false, as the Raspberry Pi
5 product in the AGL layer does. AAOS 17 puts an app that does not
declare itself automotive in the safe region with a letterbox around it,
and SurfaceFlinger then composes every layer on the GPU, so the video's
own layer is no use. On this board's 1280x720 display the safe region is
as wide as the screen but leaves a band above and below, so the
letterbox is there too. With the value false (a runtime test overlay),
all of SurfaceFlinger's layers became DEVICE on the Raspberry Pi 5
(2026-10-16); a full-screen app then covers the whole display, with no
band. On this board, with the RRO in DomA's image, a WebView's 720p
video full screen was composed as three DEVICE layers (2026-10-23); no
run without the RRO was compared here.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending [automotive-grade-linux/Android_device_sodev_xenvm-cf]
